      "content": "Mahatma Gandhi (1869–1948)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Mahatma Gandhi (1869–1948) spearheaded the non-violent freedom struggle in India.",
        "Subhas Chandra Bose (1897–1945) established leadership in the Indian National Army (Azad Hind Fauj).",
        "Bhagat Singh (1907–1931) remains a prominent symbol of revolutionary nationalism.",
        "The 'Lal-Bal-Pal' nationalist trio consisted of Lala Lajpat Rai (1865–1928), Bal Gangadhar Tilak (1856–1920), and Bipin Chandra Pal (1858–1932).",
        "Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel (1875–1950) and Jawaharlal Nehru (1889–1964) were pivotal figures in nation-building and Indian administration."
      ],
